From: YOUR NAME <your@email>
Subject: [PATCH] ieee802154: hwsim: fix double free when deleting a radio during scan

hwsim_del() frees phy->pib before ieee802154_unregister_hw().  That call
closes the slave interface, which aborts an ongoing scan and calls back
into hwsim_hw_channel() -> hwsim_update_pib().  The latter installs a new
PIB and frees the old one, so the kfree_rcu() in hwsim_del() later frees
the same object a second time:

  BUG: KASAN: double-free in kvfree_call_rcu
   ...
   hwsim_update_pib+0x276/0x400
     drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c:119
   hwsim_hw_channel+0x178/0x2b0
     drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c:131
   ...
   hwsim_del+0x49c/0x500
     drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c:1016

Free the PIB after the hardware has been unregistered, re-reading
phy->pib under pib_lock so that a PIB installed during teardown is freed
exactly once.

Fixes: 979d5b8de8ed ("ieee802154: hwsim: serialize pib updates to fix double-free")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Reported-by: syzbot+8a8482d4c33cc58babb4@syzkaller.appspotmail.com
Closes: https://syzkaller.appspot.com/bug?extid=8a8482d4c33cc58babb4
Signed-off-by: YOUR NAME <your@email>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ieee802154/mac802154_hwsim.c
@@ -1007,14 +1007,26 @@
 	list_for_each_entry_rcu(e, &phy->edges, list) {
 		list_del_rcu(&e->list);
 		hwsim_free_edge(e);
 	}
-	pib = rcu_dereference(phy->pib);
-	rcu_read_unlock();
-
-	kfree_rcu(pib, rcu);
+	rcu_read_unlock();
 
 	ieee802154_unregister_hw(phy->hw);
+
+	/*
+	 * Unregistering the hardware closes the slave interface, which aborts
+	 * an ongoing scan and calls back into hwsim_hw_channel().  That
+	 * replaces phy->pib, so re-read the pointer here and free the PIB that
+	 * is current after teardown exactly once, instead of double-freeing
+	 * the one sampled before unregistering.
+	 */
+	spin_lock_bh(&phy->pib_lock);
+	pib = rcu_replace_pointer(phy->pib, NULL,
+				  lockdep_is_held(&phy->pib_lock));
+	spin_unlock_bh(&phy->pib_lock);
+	if (pib)
+		kfree_rcu(pib, rcu);
+
 	ieee802154_free_hw(phy->hw);
 }
 
 static int hwsim_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
